      "title": "The word move is not a complete instruction",
      "narration": "David changes jobs and asks to move retirement money. First identify the arrangement sending the funds, the arrangement receiving them and whether the money is pretax, after-tax or Roth. A properly completed eligible rollover can preserve tax deferral, but a pretax-to-Roth conversion generally recognizes the previously untaxed amount as income. A receiving employer plan is not required to accept every rollover. Also confirm whether David is entitled to a distribution under the sending plan. Wanting a different investment does not by itself create a withdrawal right. The correct process starts with eligible accounts and an eligible transaction, before anyone requests a check.",
