      "title": "A direct transfer keeps payment between the institutions",
      "narration": "If Rosa moves a traditional individual retirement account directly from one trustee to another, the trustee-to-trustee transfer is not an owner-received sixty-day rollover. It is not restricted by the individual-account one-rollover-per-year rule. For an eligible employer-plan distribution, a direct rollover sends payment to the receiving retirement arrangement and avoids mandatory twenty percent withholding on that direct payment. A check can still qualify as direct when it is payable to the receiving plan or account for the owner's benefit, even if the owner forwards the check. Distinguish who is named as payee from who physically carries the envelope. Obtain the institutions' instructions and preserve the transaction records.",
