      "title": "Withholding creates a funding gap for a full rollover",
      "narration": "David receives a fifty thousand dollar eligible rollover distribution from a pretax employer plan, paid to him personally. Assume the usual twenty percent withholding applies. Ten thousand dollars goes to withholding and he receives forty thousand dollars. To roll over the entire fifty thousand dollars within the ordinary deadline, he must contribute the forty thousand received plus ten thousand from other funds. If he rolls over only forty thousand, the unrolled ten thousand remains taxable under these assumptions. The withheld amount is a tax payment credited on the return; it does not automatically satisfy the full rollover. Also do not treat withholding as the final tax owed.",
