      "title": "The 12-month period is measured from receipt",
      "text": "The covered IRA rollover limit is generally measured from the date the owner receives the distribution that is rolled over. It applies across the owner’s applicable traditional, Roth, SEP and SIMPLE arrangements, with separate eligibility restrictions. The exclusions include trustee transfers, conversions and plan-to-IRA, IRA-to-plan and plan-to-plan rollovers.",
